            <ArticleTitle>Plasma sRAGE is independently associated with high sensitivity C-reactive protein in type 2 diabetes without coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e19-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.diabres.2009.12.005</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Our studies suggest that plasma soluble advanced glycation end products (sRAGEs) has significantly negative association with high sensitivity C-reactive protein (hs-CRP) in 245 type 2 diabetes patients without diagnosed coronary artery disease (CAD). sRAGE maybe act as a novel biomarker for predicting the atherosclerosis in diabetes at the early stage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
